                <pb facs="0390" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg386"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115 Hunt Company, William/42: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-29T19:00:00-04:00">June 29, 1938—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>194. Your 318, June 27, 11 a.m., in regard to hoisting of American flag over
                    China Merchants’ property at Kiukiang. Your request approved. It is suggested
                    that, if you find that the Chinese Government did in fact issue instructions to
                    the Kiukiang manager to hoist the American flag over China Merchants’ properties
                    there, you ask the Chinese Foreign Office to have that instruction cancelled.
                    Please report further developments.</p>
                <p>Please repeat to Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
